  <diagram id="02-correcting-a-published-figure" name="02-correcting-a-published-figure" description="A decision tree. A yellow question at the top left asks: was the change expected. An arrow marked yes goes right to a green box: a revision, expected, not an error. An arrow marked no goes down to a wide blue box: a correction, an error, to be graded by what it does to the conclusions already drawn. Three arrows go down from it to three boxes. Significant, contradicts earlier conclusions: put a prominent alert on the website, correct it as soon as possible, and tell users and stakeholders. Minor but significant, insubstantial but needs correcting now in professional judgement: amend the release and show the revision clearly in it. Minor but insignificant, reasonably deemed inconsequential: correct it at the next scheduled release.">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="680" pageHeight="658" math="0" shadow="0" background="#FFFFFF">
